			steps = {
				{ title = "Learn Mining", tip = "Any Mining trainer of your faction teaches Apprentice Mining at any level (10c), and so does the Junior Mining Trainer in each starting area; the arrow picks the nearest. Buy a Mining Pick from a trade goods or general vendor: keep it in your bags, you cannot mine without it. Turn on Find Minerals (spellbook, General tab) so veins show on the minimap. Forever's starting areas also have Poor Copper Veins (Copper Ore and Rough Stone, from skill 1). The first-hour quest of each starting area (Rascally Rodents, Coldridge Valley Mail Delivery, The Woodland Protector, Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise, A Humble Task, Marla's Last Wish) offers Mining for Dummies as a reward: reading it gives 2 skill, up to 15. Trade goods vendors and the junior trainers sell the Apprentice's Mining Pack, a four-slot bag for ore and stone (25c). If you sat at your starting area's campfire for The Great Outdoors, the camping guide there also offers Camping 101: Mining: hand it in to the mining trainer it names once you reach skill 20, for the Lodestone recipe.", section = { title = "Mining 1-65", min = 1, max = 65, profession = "Mining" }, zone = 1455, goals = {
