			steps = {
				{ title = "Clavicus Knavingham, the cloth quartermaster", tip = "Clavicus Knavingham takes cloth for Stormwind. The arrow leads to him; he stands upstairs inside his building. Each first donation of 60 Wool, Silk, Mageweave and Runecloth pays 150 reputation once; after the Runecloth one, Additional Runecloth pays 50 for every 20 Runecloth, as often as you like. The Auction House is the quickest source of cloth. In Classic, quests pay full reputation while they are at most 5 levels below you, so do Elwynn (levels 1-10), Westfall (10-18), Redridge (15-25) and Duskwood (20-30) while you level through them. After the donations come the level 52-58 quests of the Western Plaguelands and the Burning Steppes (about 1,150), then the optional low-level hubs, best rate first: Northshire and the city errands (about 40 a minute at full value), the Stockade (30), Eastvale and Goldshire (25). Every Stormwind gain also gives a quarter as much to Ironforge, Darnassus and the Gnomeregan Exiles, except quests in the level 1-10 start areas. Legacy Diplomat adds up to 10% to every gain.", zone = 1453, goals = {
